    /// Disallow the use of implied `eval()`.
    ///
    /// It's considered a bad practice to pass a string to the timer functions
    /// `setTimeout`, `setInterval`, and `setImmediate`. When a string is used as
    /// the first argument, it is compiled and executed in the same way as
    /// `eval()`, which is a form of implied `eval()`. This can lead to security
    /// vulnerabilities and performance issues because the string has to be
